<section id="current" class="chapter"><div class="chapter-title"><span class="index">02</span><div><h2>Current, with a date attached</h2><p class="deck">Stable {verified.toolchain} · edition {verified.edition} · re-verified on every build</p></div></div>
<p>This edition targets <strong>Rust {verified.toolchain}</strong>, released 12 November 2026. Every example on this page was compiled by <code>{verified.rustc}</code> when the site was built. A Rust program, <code>studio-verify</code>, checks each one against its declared outcome and refuses to publish a stale result. The starter pins the same exact compiler. <strong>2024 is the edition name, not the year of your compiler.</strong> New projects should use <code>edition = "2024"</code>; upgrading an existing repository deserves its own migration and tests.</p>
<div class="callout"><h3>What changed in 1.100?</h3><p>The never type <code>!</code> is stable: you can name it, as in <code>Result&lt;T, !&gt;</code>, and <code>std::convert::Infallible</code> is now an alias for it. A function can now say in its signature that it cannot fail, and callers can write an irrefutable <code>let Ok(value) = …</code> with no Err arm. The release also stabilizes the <code>Allocator</code> API, <code>core::mem::DropGuard</code>, and smaller conveniences such as <code>bool::toggle</code> and <code>str::trim_prefix</code>.</p><p>Cargo now warns about unused dependencies by default (configurable under <code>[lints.cargo]</code>) and changes its internal build-directory layout. Final artifacts such as <code>target/debug/signal-notebook</code> stay where they were; this site's own build was checked against that.</p><p>Those are release notes, not prerequisites. The examples stay in safe, stable Rust.</p></div>
<Example name="never" />
<p><strong>Freshness boundary:</strong> the compiler results update whenever the pin changes; the prose is a researched snapshot as of 12 November 2026. Before future work, run <code>rustup check</code>, read release notes, and update deliberately. A toolchain pin changes only when you edit it.</p>
